REM ==========================================================================
REM switchover.dgmgrl
REM
REM Purpose:
REM   Template for a PLANNED switchover: the primary and standby swap
REM   roles with no data loss, typically for maintenance or testing.
REM   Validation runs before the switch, and the configuration is
REM   shown again after it.
REM
REM Usage:
REM   dgmgrl / @switchover.dgmgrl
REM
REM   Replace <STANDBY_DB_UNIQUE_NAME> with the standby database's
REM   DB_UNIQUE_NAME before running.
REM
REM WARNING:
REM   A switchover reverses the roles of the primary and standby.
REM   Application connections follow the new primary only if the
REM   service configuration points them there, so plan the connection
REM   cutover alongside this command. Do not run this against a
REM   database you care about until the runbook in
REM   docs/switchover-failover-runbook.md has been walked through on
REM   a lab configuration. If VALIDATE DATABASE reports an error,
REM   fix it first; do not force the switchover past a failed
REM   validation.
REM
REM Notes:
REM   A switchover requires the standby to be in sync, which is why
REM   the validation step comes first. After the switch, the old
REM   primary becomes the new standby and begins applying redo in
REM   the other direction, so there is a path back.
REM   Reviewed; not executed against a live Oracle instance.
REM ==========================================================================

CONNECT /
VALIDATE DATABASE '<STANDBY_DB_UNIQUE_NAME>';
SWITCHOVER TO '<STANDBY_DB_UNIQUE_NAME>';
SHOW CONFIGURATION;
EXIT;
